ation":{"args":{"before":"test('mix: a COMMENT is trivia anywhere — between a table\\'s fields, a call\\'s arguments', function ()","after":"test('mix: a NON-FINITE number reaching dynamic code is lifted as the division that makes it — 1/0, -1/0, 0/0', function ()\n    ready()\n    local src = 'local function f(x)\\n    local best, worst = math.huge, -math.huge\\n    if x < best then best = x end\\n    if x > worst then worst = x end\\n    return best, worst\\nend\\n'\n    local r, text = residual(src, 'f', { 'D' }, {})\n    for _, x in ipairs({ -3, 0, 7 }) do\n        local b, w = r(x)\n        local ob, ow = original(src, 'f')(x)\n        eq(ob, b); eq(ow, w)\n    end\n    ok(text:find('(1 / 0)', 1, true) and text:find('(-1 / 0)', 1, true), text)\nend)\n\ntest('mix: a COMMENT is trivia anywhere — between a table\\'s fields, a call\\'s arguments', function ()","file":"tests/mix_spec.lua"},"touched":["tests/mix_spec.lua"],"verb":"edit"},"decisions":[],"verb":"edit"},{"id":"1791133066.440678-edit","bytes":10540,"decided_by":"tactic","invocation":{"args":{"before":"Refused by name: while, varargs, a closure capturing a per-iteration loop local or assigning a captured PARAMETER,","after":"LOOPS (CART-1450 rung 1, 2026-10-04): `while` / `repeat` / `break` — a loop whose condition is static UNROLLS (the unfold budget bounds one that never ends, by name), a dynamic one stays a residual loop; a STATIC break ends the unrolling and leaves nothing; a DYNAMIC break puts the unrolled iterations in `repeat … until true`, and its CONGRUENCE makes every store in that loop's body dynamic (the code after the loop sees one of several exits — a static `s = s + v` after `if v == x then break end` would sum every element); a COMMENT is trivia in every position (`named` drops it — before, one between a lambda's parameters and its body made the body position read the comment and the lambda lowered EMPTY, silently: CART-1451); a non-finite number lifts as `1/0`, `-1/0`, `0/0`. PINS: a closure capturing a PER-ITERATION local (a loop variable, a local of a loop body) COPIES it when the closure is made (`lam.pin`, read through `MX.cval`), so a closure made in iteration i sees iteration i's value, called during the loop or after it; refused by name: a pinned local the loop body assigns AFTER the first capture (textually after, its right-hand side included, or in a loop nested in its scope — an assignment written before the capture is fine), and a closure over a DYNAMIC per-iteration local used after its iteration (its residual name would be out of scope: every loop body is specialized inside an ITERATION SCOPE). MEASURED: on 13 hot modules (973 functions, 29,114 lines) 412 functions / 5,590 lines (19%) are in S with every parameter dynamic, vs 16% truly at HEAD (HEAD's census said 27%: 40 functions / 3,139 lines counted in S had their body dropped by a comment); 31 of derive.lua's 36 derivations lower clean (19 before). 10/10 mutations caught. Refused by name: varargs, goto, a closure assigning a captured PARAMETER or loop variable,","file":".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"},"touched":[".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"],"verb":"edit"},"decisions":[],"verb":"edit"},{"id":"1791133066.515935-edit","bytes":1547,"decided_by":"tactic","invocation":{"args":{"before":"file-level CONSTANTS (Q, HEDK, CTXK) and match's debug env reads are not assembled.","after":"file-level CONSTANTS (Q, HEDK, CTXK) and match's debug env reads are not assembled. 2026-10-04 (CART-1450 pins): 31 of 36 derivations lower clean — the per-iteration captures are PINNED; left: 3 nested non-local function declarations, WF_PATH, an assignment to B.","file":".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"},"touched":[".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"],"verb":"edit"},"decisions":[],"verb":"edit"},{"id":"1791133074.716457-edit","bytes":318,"decided_by":"tactic","invocation":{"args":{"before":"-- REFUSED by name, never residualized silentl