s as `1/0`, `-1/0`, `0/0`. PINS: a closure capturing a PER-ITERATION local (a loop variable, a local of a loop body) COPIES it when the closure is made (`lam.pin`, read through `MX.cval`), so a closure made in iteration i sees iteration i's value, called during the loop or after it; refused by name: a pinned local the loop body assigns AFTER the first capture (textually after, its right-hand side included, or in a loop nested in its scope — an assignment written before the capture is fine), and a closure over a DYNAMIC per-iteration local used after its iteration (its residual name would be out of scope: every loop body is specialized inside an ITERATION SCOPE). MEASURED: on 13 hot modules (973 functions, 29,114 lines) 412 functions / 5,590 lines (19%) are in S with every parameter dynamic, vs 16% truly at HEAD (HEAD's census said 27%: 40 functions / 3,139 lines counted in S had their body dropped by a comment); 31 of derive.lua's 36 derivations lower clean (19 before). 10/10 mutations caught. Refused by name: varargs, goto, a closure assigning a captured PARAMETER or loop variable,","file":".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"},"touched":[".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"],"verb":"edit"},"id":"1791133066.440678-edit","verb":"edit"},{"invocation":{"args":{"before":"file-level CONSTANTS (Q, HEDK, CTXK) and match's debug env reads are not assembled.","after":"file-level CONSTANTS (Q, HEDK, CTXK) and match's debug env reads are not assembled. 2026-10-04 (CART-1450 pins): 31 of 36 derivations lower clean — the per-iteration captures are PINNED; left: 3 nested non-local function declarations, WF_PATH, an assignment to B.","file":".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"},"touched":[".claude/skills/cartograph/references/questions.md"],"verb":"edit"},"id":"1791133066.515935-edit","verb":"edit"},{"invocation":{"args":{"before":"-- REFUSED by name, never residualized silently: varargs, goto, method calls, metatables (not in S);\n-- a